          <fr:mainmatter><html:p>This blog will function both as a worklog and a release for my <fr:link href="/060Z/" title="Pallas" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/060Z/" display-uri="060Z" type="local">Pallas</fr:link> implementation of <fr:link href="/dongFlexAttentionProgramming2024/" title="Flex Attention: A Programming Model for Generating Optimized Attention Kernels" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/dongFlexAttentionProgramming2024/" display-uri="dongFlexAttentionProgramming2024" type="local">FlexAttention</fr:link> on <fr:link href="/NZZ7/" title="TPU Architecture" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/NZZ7/" display-uri="NZZ7" type="local">TPU Architecture</fr:link>. </html:p><html:figure><html:img width="80%" src="/bafkrmig6ozqvm3pbwzvn6lbpirgxmsd36qwlcma2htsj4xtyxh6v3uft5e.png" />
<html:figcaption>ChatGPT realizing my weird brain child.</html:figcaption></html:figure><html:p>As a pre-cursor, I highly recommend reading the original <fr:link href="/dongFlexAttentionProgramming2024/" title="Flex Attention: A Programming Model for Generating Optimized Attention Kernels" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/dongFlexAttentionProgramming2024/" display-uri="dongFlexAttentionProgramming2024" type="local">FlexAttention paper</fr:link>. Additionally, a big shout out to the people at google for <fr:link href="/splash_attention/" title="Splash attention: Sparse flash attention for TPU" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/splash_attention/" display-uri="splash_attention" type="local">SplashAttention</fr:link>, which we unfortunately aim to make obsolete as a subset of flex attention. For a very deep dive on splash attention, I <html:strong>highly</html:strong> recommend <fr:link href="/toulme2026xla/" title="When XLA isn’t enough: From Pallas to VLIW with Splash attention on TPU" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/toulme2026xla/" display-uri="toulme2026xla" type="local">this blog</fr:link>. We will cover the key implementation details to accentuate our work here.</html:p>
